    <!-- APP 1 -->
    <section id="king-of-beasts" class="band" aria-labelledby="app1-title">
      <div class="band__inner">
        <h2 id="app1-title" class="display display--sm">The King of Beasts</h2>
        <div class="app">
          <img class="app__icon" src="/app-king-of-beasts.png" width="128" height="128" alt="The King of Beasts app icon: a crowned white lion surrounded by fire, nature, earth, and water." loading="lazy">
          <div class="prose">
            <p><strong>King of Beasts is a strategy battle game for iPhone. You raise one beast and fight your way up the ladder to become king.</strong></p>
            <p>Pick a home element: Fire, Water, Earth, Air, Spirit, Poison, Light or Dark. Or go Natural and let raw strength do the work. Then build your beast&rsquo;s attacks and defenses from the elements you win. Some elements counter others, and some pairs combine into powers you have to discover for yourself.</p>
            <p>Every round is a secret guess. Attack, Guard or Shift, and each one beats another. Before a fight you can study your opponent&rsquo;s recent battles and tune your build to counter them. Or you can change your own pattern so you can&rsquo;t be read.</p>
            <p>Power is never handed out. Win a battle and you take 1 unit of power from your opponent. Battle is the only way a beast grows. Climb five tiers, from Beginner to Expert, and every step up brings more strategy.</p>
            <p>Play the computer to train, or challenge a friend face to face on a second phone. Nothing in the game can be bought to make a beast stronger. Purchases only unlock extra beast slots.</p>
            <p><strong>Status:</strong> TestFlight beta.</p>
            <p><a class="link-arrow" href="https://testflight.apple.com/join/Kqr1X4cr" rel="noopener">Join the beta on TestFlight <span aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span></a></p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- APP 2 -->
    <section id="war-of-the-4-kings" class="band band--sand" aria-labelledby="app2-title">
      <div class="band__inner">
        <h2 id="app2-title" class="display display--sm">War of the 4 Kings</h2>
        <div class="app">
          <img class="app__icon" src="/app-war-of-the-4-kings.png" width="128" height="128" alt="War of the 4 Kings app icon: a gold crown over a diamond split into red, green, black, and gold quarters." loading="lazy">
          <div class="prose">
            <p><strong>Four armies. Four Kings. One table. Be the last player holding cards.</strong></p>
            <p>War of the 4 Kings is a card game of battles, betrayal and long memories. You are one of the four Kings, leading a Red, Green, Black or Gold army across the table. Each round, every player places a card on the battlefield face down. The highest card wins the battle and takes everything on it.</p>
            <p>Then the Heroes arrive. A General collects hostages from every loser. A Spy that falls to a General can steal him away. A Medic saves a fallen card before it reaches the graveyard. An Assassin ends a Hero with a single card. When one player holds all the power, the others can call a revolt and match a card to cancel it.</p>
            <p>If the table stalls, the Army of the Dead rises from the graveyard and joins the fight as a player of its own. The game ends when one King is left holding cards.</p>
            <p>Play 3 or 4 players. Take on the computer armies at three difficulty levels, each with its own style of play.</p>
            <p><strong>Status:</strong> TestFlight beta.</p>
            <p><a class="link-arrow" href="https://testflight.apple.com/join/HgCzJJs7" rel="noopener">Join the beta on TestFlight <span aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span></a></p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- APP 3 -->
    <section id="check-my-list" class="band" aria-labelledby="app3-title">
      <div class="band__inner">
        <h2 id="app3-title" class="display display--sm">Check My List: Routines</h2>
        <div class="app">
          <img class="app__icon" src="/app-check-my-list.png" width="128" height="128" alt="Check My List: Routines app icon: a clipboard with two checked items and one open item." loading="lazy">
          <div class="prose">
            <p><strong>Your calendar knows when. Check My List knows what to do before.</strong></p>
            <p>Check My List turns your calendar into a plan for getting ready.</p>
            <p>Most calendars tell you what&rsquo;s happening and when. They don&rsquo;t tell you to pack the shin guards, fill the water bottle, or leave by 4:15 to get there on time. Check My List does. It reads the events already on your iPhone calendar and figures out what kind each one is: a soccer game, a cross country meet, a concert, a youth group night, a road trip. Then it builds a checklist of timed steps, counted back from the start time.</p>
            <p>You check steps off as you finish them, and the app reminds you about the ones still waiting. It also works out bedtime backward from tomorrow&rsquo;s first event, then builds a wind-down routine for the evening so the morning starts calmly.</p>
            <p>It was built for a busy kid with a full week, and it works for anyone who has somewhere to be and a list of things to do first.</p>
            <p><strong>Status:</strong> TestFlight beta.</p>
            <p><a class="link-arrow" href="https://testflight.apple.com/join/sxv2UYap" rel="noopener">Join the beta on TestFlight <span aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span></a></p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
